---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArchitectureDiagram from "../components/ArchitectureDiagram.astro";
import BenchmarkExplorer from "../components/BenchmarkExplorer.astro";
import { loadEvidence } from "../lib/evidence";

const evidence = loadEvidence();
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Hanoi Local Zone Field Notes — An evidence-driven AWS lab"
  description="A measured comparison of Singapore, Hanoi Local Zone, and a hybrid Singapore-to-Hanoi PostgreSQL path—built from 1,200 retained AWS requests."
>
  <section class="hero shell">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="hero-meta">
        <span class="status-pill">AWS_REAL · NOT_DEPLOYED</span>
        <span>Historical run · 1,200 requests · 0 errors</span>
      </div>
      <p class="eyebrow">AWS Hanoi Local Zone · Engineering field notes</p>
      <h1 class="display-title">Moving the database closer made the app <em>slower.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        We measured three real request paths from Vietnam. Hanoi reduced client latency in this run—but a Singapore API talking sequentially to Hanoi PostgreSQL turned one network boundary into twenty waits.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}insights/what-1200-requests-taught-us/`}>Read in English</a>
        <a class="button" lang="vi" href={`${base}insights/aws-hanoi-local-zone-1200-requests-3-kien-truc/`}>Đọc tiếng Việt</a>
        <a class="button" href={`${base}evidence/`}>Explore the measurements</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="hero-result" aria-label="Key retained benchmark result">
      <div class="result-head">
        <span>Hybrid DB p50</span>
        <span>Sequential SQL</span>
      </div>
      <div class="amplification">
        <div><span>1 query</span><strong>36</strong><small>ms</small></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <div><span>20 queries</span><strong>719</strong><small>ms</small></div>
      </div>
      <p>About 20× the database time for 20 sequential cross-location queries.</p>
      <div class="mini-bars" aria-hidden="true">
        <span style="--height: 5%"></span><span style="--height: 25%"></span><span style="--height: 50%"></span><span style="--height: 100%"></span>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="truth-band" aria-label="Evidence provenance">
    <div class="shell truth-grid">
      <div><span>Current AWS state</span><strong>NOT_DEPLOYED</strong></div>
      <div><span>Historical evidence</span><strong>{evidence.measuredRequests.toLocaleString("en-US")} requests</strong></div>
      <div><span>Measured errors</span><strong>0 / 1,200</strong></div>
      <div><span>Active project cost</span><strong>$0 / hour</strong></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">01 · The experiment</p>
        <h2>Two machines. Three architectures.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The cost-minimal lab used one EC2 instance in Singapore and one in Hanoi. Three logical paths isolate what changes when application locality, database locality, or both move.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ArchitectureDiagram />
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">02 · The evidence</p>
        <h2>Locality helped—until the tiers split.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Toggle scenarios and metrics. Hide Hybrid to rescale Singapore and Hanoi; switch to DB p50 to see sequential cross-location work dominate the request.
      </p>
    </div>
    <BenchmarkExplorer evidence={evidence} compact />
  </section>

  <section class="section shell lessons">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">03 · What survived contact with AWS</p>
        <h2>The benchmark was only half the lesson.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>The deployment failures exposed the operational details architecture sketches tend to hide.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lesson-grid">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>An AZ-like name is not an S3 Region.</h3>
        <p>Hanoi bootstrap failed when a Local Zone identifier was treated like an S3 endpoint. Artifacts lived in the Singapore parent Region.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Terraform validate cannot test provider reality.</h3>
        <p>A 12 GiB root passed validation but could not launch from a 30 GiB AMI snapshot. Runtime constraints still need evidence.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Your presenter network is infrastructure input.</h3>
        <p>Cloudflare WARP changed the exact `/32` egress address and invalidated a reviewed plan. The safe response was to stop, not widen ingress.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Cleanup deserves architecture.</h3>
        <p>Protected EBS and versioned S3 made deletion deliberate. The final audit checked AWS APIs independently before declaring zero active cost.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="button-row lesson-cta">
      <a class="button" href={`${base}field-notes/`}>Read the engineering field notes</a>
      <a class="button" href={`${base}architecture/`}>Inspect the architecture</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell final-thesis">
    <p class="eyebrow">The durable conclusion</p>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Latency is a property of the whole synchronous path—not a Region label and not one resource.</p>
    </blockquote>
    <div>
      <p>
        Colocate chatty tiers, reduce sequential work, and make evidence provenance visible. A Local Zone can improve locality, but it does not automatically provide availability, residency, or application performance.
      </p>
      <a href={`${base}insights/what-1200-requests-taught-us/`}>Continue to the full analysis →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    min-height: min(880px, calc(100vh - 76px));
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(340px, 0.75fr);
    gap: clamp(48px, 8vw, 120px);
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: clamp(72px, 11vw, 140px);
  }

  .hero-meta {
    display: flex;
    margin-bottom: 58px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 14px 20px;
    align-items: center;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 920px;
    font-size: clamp(4.2rem, 9.8vw, 9.1rem);
  }

  .hero h1 em {
    color: var(--orange);
    font-weight: inherit;
  }

  .hero-lede {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 32px 0;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .hero-result {
    align-self: end;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--hybrid);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 24px;
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }

  .result-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .amplification {
    display: grid;
    margin-block: 28px 18px;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: end;
  }

  .amplification div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto auto;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .amplification span {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
  }

  .amplification strong {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 6vw, 5.8rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.07em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .amplification small {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .amplification i {
    width: 28px;
    height: 1px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    background: var(--line-bright);
  }

  .hero-result > p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .mini-bars {
    display: flex;
    height: 72px;
    margin-top: 22px;
    gap: 7px;
    align-items: end;
  }

  .mini-bars span {
    width: 25%;
    height: var(--height);
    background: var(--hybrid);
    opacity: 0.72;
  }

  .truth-band {
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: #080d18;
  }

  .truth-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  }

  .truth-grid div {
    display: grid;
    min-height: 112px;
    align-content: center;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .truth-grid div:first-child {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .truth-grid span {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .truth-grid strong {
    color: var(--green);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .lesson-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .lesson-grid article {
    min-height: 300px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: clamp(24px, 5vw, 52px);
    background: rgba(12, 18, 32, 0.7);
  }

  .lesson-grid span {
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
  }

  .lesson-grid h3 {
    max-width: 460px;
    margin: 46px 0 16px;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.6rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.08;
  }

  .lesson-grid p {
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .lesson-cta {
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .final-thesis {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(120px, 0.4fr) minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(260px, 0.8fr);
    gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 80px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .final-thesis blockquote {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .final-thesis blockquote p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 5.5rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.02;
  }

  .final-thesis > div {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .final-thesis a {
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .hero-result {
      width: min(100%, 520px);
      align-self: auto;
    }

    .truth-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .final-thesis {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .hero {
      min-height: auto;
      padding-top: 56px;
    }

    .hero-meta {
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 17vw, 5.4rem);
    }

    .truth-grid,
    .lesson-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .truth-grid div,
    .truth-grid div:first-child {
      border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .lesson-grid article {
      min-height: 250px;
    }
  }
</style>
